# ---- merge-sweep budget (optional — hub only) ----
# bin/merge-sweep.sh merges at most this many VERIFIED tier-2 PRs per pass,
# fleet-wide across every repo it sweeps. Default 5. The walk that spends it is
# round-robin across projects, newest record first (BH-710), so the slots land
# on up to N different repos before any repo gets a second one. Only a
# confirmed MERGED spends budget — a
# skip, a park, an enqueue and a failed attempt all cost nothing. A non-numeric
# value logs one line and falls back to 5; 0 attempts nothing (the kill switch
# is still flags/automerge-disabled). The sweep sources this file, so the value
# here and SWEEP_MERGE_BUDGET in the process env are the same knob — a value set
# in both resolves to this file's. docs/verification-map/merge-sweep-budget.md
#SWEEP_MERGE_BUDGET=5

